IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mhw-dates`

-- Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) -- the rules the questions share: the s 3 kinds of patient and the orders,
-- s 4 mental illness, the s 142 and s 143 criteria, s 87 capacity, what the Mental Health Tribunal must do with an
-- order (ss 192, 194, 204, 207), and the duties with deadlines that the Act puts on the Tribunal, the authorised
-- psychiatrist and the chief psychiatrist, run as regulative rules.
--
-- This module holds the law that more than one question uses. The questions are asked in mhw-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it;
-- where a section is used by one question only, the seat module applies its words there and cites them. Nothing here
-- is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "must not", "may only
-- ... if", "cannot", an "if" condition that fails, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The judgments the Act hands to practitioners, the authorised
-- psychiatrist, the chief psychiatrist, the Tribunal and VCAT ("satisfied", "appears", "reasonably considers",
-- "exceptional circumstances", "special circumstances") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Mental Health
-- and Wellbeing Act 2022, Version No. 010 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS
    IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3 -- the orders and the kinds of patient`

-- The order the person is subject to. s 3(1): an "assessment patient" is subject to an assessment order (s 144); a
-- "court assessment patient" to a court assessment order (Sentencing Act 1991 s 90); a "temporary treatment patient" to
-- a temporary treatment order (s 180); a "treatment patient" to a treatment order (s 192(2)(a)); a "security patient" is
-- detained in a designated mental health service under a secure treatment order or court secure treatment order; a
-- "forensic patient" is one under the Crimes (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997 (borrowed, asked).
DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `no order`
    `an assessment order`
    `a court assessment order`
    `a temporary treatment order`
    `a treatment order`
    `a secure treatment order or court secure treatment order`
    `a forensic patient order`

-- s 3(1) "patient means -- (a) an assessment patient; or (b) a court assessment patient; or (c) a temporary treatment
-- patient; or (d) a treatment patient; or (e) a security patient; or (f) a forensic patient". A "means" definition.
GIVEN o IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a patient` o IF
    NOT (o EQUALS `no order`)

-- s 3(1) "eligible patient means -- (a) a temporary treatment patient; or (b) a treatment patient; or (c) a security
-- patient; or (d) a forensic patient". A "means" definition. (The eligible patient may seek a second opinion, s 67.)
GIVEN o IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- an eligible patient` o IF
        o EQUALS `a temporary treatment order`
     OR o EQUALS `a treatment order`
     OR o EQUALS `a secure treatment order or court secure treatment order`
     OR o EQUALS `a forensic patient order`

-- s 3(1) "young patient means a patient who is under the age of 18 years"; "young person means -- (a) in Chapter 3, a
-- person under 18 years of age".
GIVEN o IS AN `Order`, `my age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a young patient` o `my age` IF
    `s 3 -- a patient` o AND `my age` LESS THAN 18

§§ `s 4 -- mental illness`

-- s 4(1) "Mental illness is a medical condition that is characterised by a significant disturbance of thought, mood,
-- perception or memory." (2) "A person is not to be considered to have mental illness by reason only of any one or more
-- of the following -- (a) ... (p)" (political, religious or philosophical opinions or activity, sexual preference,
-- gender identity or orientation, sexual behaviour, conduct contrary to community standards, illegal conduct,
-- antisocial behaviour, intellectual disability, drug or alcohol use, economic or social status, cultural or racial
-- group, family conflict, psychological distress, a past diagnosis or treatment). (3) "Subsection (2)(l) does not prevent
-- the serious temporary or permanent physiological, biochemical or psychological effects of using drugs or alcohol from
-- being regarded as an indication that a person has mental illness." A definition and a flat negative: JUST FALSE where
-- either fails. Whether a condition is "significant" is a clinical judgment, asked.
GIVEN `a medical condition significantly disturbing thought, mood, perception or memory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only grounds are s 4(2) matters`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is the serious effects of drugs or alcohol`                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- mental illness` `a medical condition significantly disturbing thought, mood, perception or memory` `the only grounds are s 4(2) matters` `the ground is the serious effects of drugs or alcohol` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    `a medical condition significantly disturbing thought, mood, perception or memory`
                 AND (NOT (`the only grounds are s 4(2) matters` AND (NOT `the ground is the serious effects of drugs or alcohol`))))

§§ `ss 142, 143 -- the criteria`

-- s 142 "The compulsory assessment criteria for a person to be made subject to an assessment order are that -- (a) the
-- person appears to have mental illness; and (b) because the person appears to have mental illness, the person appears
-- to need immediate treatment to prevent -- (i) serious deterioration in the person's mental or physical health; or (ii)
-- serious harm to the person or to another person; and (c) if the person is made subject to an assessment order, the
-- person can be assessed; and (d) there are no less restrictive means reasonably available to enable the person to be
-- assessed." Each limb is the practitioner's view, asked.
GIVEN `I appear to have mental illness`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I appear to need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can be assessed under the order`                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `no less restrictive means to assess me`                       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 142 -- the compulsory assessment criteria apply` `I appear to have mental illness` `I appear to need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm` `I can be assessed under the order` `no less restrictive means to assess me` IF
        `I appear to have mental illness`
    AND `I appear to need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm`
    AND `I can be assessed under the order`
    AND `no less restrictive means to assess me`

-- s 143 "The compulsory treatment criteria for a person to be made subject to a temporary treatment order or treatment
-- order are that -- (a) the person has mental illness; and (b) because the person has mental illness, the person needs
-- immediate treatment to prevent -- (i) serious deterioration in the person's mental or physical health; or (ii) serious
-- harm to the person or to another person; and (c) if the person is made subject to a temporary treatment order or
-- treatment order, the immediate treatment will be provided to the person; and (d) there are no less restrictive means
-- reasonably available to enable the person to receive the immediate treatment."
GIVEN `I have mental illness`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the treatment will be provided under the order`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `no less restrictive means to treat me`                        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 143 -- the compulsory treatment criteria apply` `I have mental illness` `I need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm` `the treatment will be provided under the order` `no less restrictive means to treat me` IF
        `I have mental illness`
    AND `I need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm`
    AND `the treatment will be provided under the order`
    AND `no less restrictive means to treat me`

§§ `s 87 -- capacity to give informed consent`

-- s 87(1) "A person has capacity to give informed consent if the person -- (a) is able to understand the information
-- they are given for the purpose of deciding whether or not to consent; and (b) is able to remember that information;
-- and (c) is able to use or weigh that information in deciding whether or not to consent; and (d) is able to communicate
-- the decision the person makes by speech, gestures or any other means." Read as a full test (fork F5): JUST FALSE
-- where a limb fails. s 85(2): capacity is presumed; s 87(2)(c), (d): not to be assumed absent only because of age,
-- appearance, disability, condition or behaviour, or an unwise decision.
GIVEN `I can understand the information`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can remember it`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can use or weigh it`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can communicate my decision`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87 -- I have capacity to give informed consent` `I can understand the information` `I can remember it` `I can use or weigh it` `I can communicate my decision` IF
        `I can understand the information`
    AND `I can remember it`
    AND `I can use or weigh it`
    AND `I can communicate my decision`

§§ `What the Mental Health Tribunal must do with an order`

DECLARE `Tribunal outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal must make or confirm the order as a community order`
    `the Tribunal must make or confirm the order, and may make it an inpatient order or a community order`
    `the Tribunal must confirm the inpatient treatment order`
    `the Tribunal must vary the order to a community treatment order`
    `the Tribunal must revoke the order`

-- s 192(2) (a hearing on a temporary treatment order, or an application for another treatment order): "must -- (a) make
-- a treatment order ... if the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that the compulsory treatment criteria apply to the
-- person; or (b) revoke the temporary treatment order or treatment order ... if the Mental Health Tribunal is not
-- satisfied"; s 194(2) "must not make an inpatient treatment order ... unless the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that
-- the person cannot be treated in the community". s 207(2), (4), (5) are the same for a revocation application.
GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tribunal outcome`
`ss 192, 194, 207 -- what the Tribunal must do` `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria apply` `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria apply`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`
         THEN `the Tribunal must make or confirm the order, and may make it an inpatient order or a community order`
         ELSE `the Tribunal must make or confirm the order as a community order`
    ELSE `the Tribunal must revoke the order`

-- s 204(3): "(a) confirm the inpatient treatment order if the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that -- (i) the
-- compulsory treatment criteria still apply to the treatment patient; and (ii) the patient cannot be treated in the
-- community; or (b) vary the order to a community treatment order if the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that -- (i)
-- the compulsory treatment criteria still apply ...; and (ii) the patient can be treated in the community; or (c) revoke
-- the treatment order if the Mental Health Tribunal is not satisfied that the compulsory treatment criteria apply". The
-- Tribunal's view on the community is asked as one yes/no (finding 3).
GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria still apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tribunal outcome`
`s 204(3) -- what the Tribunal must do` `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria still apply` `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria still apply`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal is satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`
         THEN `the Tribunal must confirm the inpatient treatment order`
         ELSE `the Tribunal must vary the order to a community treatment order`
    ELSE `the Tribunal must revoke the order`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`
    `not owed on these facts`

DECLARE `Duty holder` IS ONE OF
    `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    `the authorised psychiatrist`
    `the chief psychiatrist`

DECLARE `Act owed` IS ONE OF
    `hold the hearing`
    `give me written reasons`
    `review my treatment`
    `give a statement of reasons`

-- s 189(1): "Before a temporary treatment order expires, the Mental Health Tribunal must conduct a hearing to determine
-- whether to make a treatment order in respect of the temporary treatment patient." Days from the day the order was
-- made; the deadline is its last day in force, with any s 374(2) extension.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    MUST `hold the hearing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Mental Health Tribunal` BECAUSE "the Tribunal did not conduct a hearing before the temporary treatment order expired (s 189(1)); the order lapses at its expiry (s 183)"

-- s 204(1): "Within 28 days after a community treatment order is varied to an inpatient treatment order, beginning on
-- and including the day the order was varied, the Mental Health Tribunal must conduct a hearing to determine whether the
-- treatment patient should be subject to an inpatient treatment order." Days from the day of the variation.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 204(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me within 28 days after my order was made inpatient` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    MUST `hold the hearing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Mental Health Tribunal` BECAUSE "the Tribunal did not conduct a hearing within 28 days, beginning on and including the day the community treatment order was varied to an inpatient treatment order (s 204(1))"

-- s 97(1): "The Mental Health Tribunal must list and complete the hearing of an application under this Part within 5
-- business days after receiving the application." (Electroconvulsive treatment.) Days from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 97(1) -- the Tribunal must hear the electroconvulsive treatment application within 5 business days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    MUST `hold the hearing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Mental Health Tribunal` BECAUSE "the Tribunal did not list and complete the hearing of the electroconvulsive treatment application within 5 business days after receiving it (s 97(1))"

-- s 124: "The Mental Health Tribunal must hear and determine an application made under section 120 within 30 business
-- days after receipt of the application." (Neurosurgery for mental illness.) Days from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 124 -- the Tribunal must determine the neurosurgery application within 30 business days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    MUST `hold the hearing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Mental Health Tribunal` BECAUSE "the Tribunal did not hear and determine the neurosurgery application within 30 business days after receiving it (s 124)"

-- ss 73(3)(b), 74(4)(b), 90(2): after a second psychiatric opinion, or on overriding an advance statement of
-- preferences, the authorised psychiatrist must give the patient written reasons "within 10 business days after the
-- determination [or decision] is made" (s 90(2): "as soon as practicable but no later than within 10 business days").
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`ss 73, 74, 90 -- the authorised psychiatrist must give me written reasons within 10 business days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the authorised psychiatrist`
    MUST `give me written reasons`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the authorised psychiatrist` BECAUSE "the authorised psychiatrist did not give the patient written reasons within 10 business days after the determination or decision (ss 73(3)(b), 74(4)(b), 90(2))"

-- s 76(1): "The chief psychiatrist must review the treatment of an eligible patient within 10 business days after
-- receiving an application under section 75(1)." Days from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 76(1) -- the chief psychiatrist must review my treatment within 10 business days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the chief psychiatrist`
    MUST `review my treatment`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the chief psychiatrist` BECAUSE "the chief psychiatrist did not review the treatment within 10 business days after receiving the application (s 76(1))"

-- s 380(4): "Within 20 business days after receiving a request under subsection (1), the Mental Health Tribunal must
-- give a statement of reasons to all parties to the proceeding for which the request was made." Days from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
`s 380(4) -- the Tribunal must give a statement of reasons within 20 business days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    MUST `give a statement of reasons`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Mental Health Tribunal` BECAUSE "the Tribunal did not give a statement of reasons within 20 business days after receiving the request (s 380(4))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (in the shape of the Coroners Act 2008 encoding's helper). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in
-- time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes
-- a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
      `who owes it`                 IS A `Duty holder`
      `what is owed`                IS AN `Act owed`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of` `the rule` `owed by` `who owes it` `to do` `what is owed` `done` `the act has been done` `at` `the time the act was done` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `who owes it` `what is owed` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `who owes it` `what is owed` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- The same, counted in days from a start date to the last day allowed.
GIVEN `the start`                   IS A DATE
      `the last day`                IS A DATE
      `the rule maker`              IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO DEONTIC `Duty holder` `Act owed`
      `who owes it`                 IS A `Duty holder`
      `what is owed`                IS AN `Act owed`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done`         IS A DATE
      `today`                       IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the duty from` `the start` `to` `the last day` `under` `the rule maker` `owed by` `who owes it` `to do` `what is owed` `done` `the act has been done` `on` `the day it was done` `as at` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` (`the rule maker` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the last day`)) `owed by` `who owes it` `to do` `what is owed` `done` `the act has been done` `at` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the day it was done`) `now` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `today`)
